{"id":"multi-head-attention","t":"Grouped-query cross-attention with key padding","tags":["Attention","Transformers"],"d":"Hard","rt":"numpy","fn":"gqa","tol":[1e-06,1e-08],"pkgs":[],"st":"Grouped-query attention (GQA) keeps $H$ query heads but only $H_{kv}$ key/value heads; each group of $H / H_{kv}$ consecutive query heads shares one key/value head. It shrinks the KV cache by a factor $H / H_{kv}$. With $H_{kv} = H$ it is ordinary multi-head attention, with $H_{kv} = 1$ it is multi-query attention.\n\nWrite `gqa(Xq, Xkv, Wq, Wk, Wv, Wo, n_heads, n_kv_heads, kv_mask=None)` for **cross**-attention (queries and keys come from different sequences).\n\n## Shapes\n- `Xq`: `(B, T_q, D)` queries' source; `Xkv`: `(B, T_k, D)` keys' and values' source.\n- $H$ = `n_heads` divides $D$; head width $d_h = D / H$. $H_{kv}$ = `n_kv_heads` divides $H$.\n- `Wq`: `(D, D)`, `Wk` and `Wv`: `(D, H_kv * d_h)`, `Wo`: `(D, D)`. No biases.\n- `kv_mask`: optional bool `(B, T_k)`, `True` for real tokens, `False` for padding. `None` means all real.\n\n## Computation\n1. $Q = X_q W_q$, $K = X_{kv} W_k$, $V = X_{kv} W_v$. Query head $h$ is columns $h d_h : (h+1) d_h$ of $Q$; KV head $g$ is columns $g d_h : (g+1) d_h$ of $K$ and $V$.\n2. Query head $h$ uses KV head $g = \\lfloor h / (H / H_{kv}) \\rfloor$.\n3. Per head: scores $Q_h K_g^\\top / \\sqrt{d_h}$, padded keys set to $-\\infty$, stable softmax over keys, times $V_g$.\n4. If a sample has **no** real keys, its attention output is all zeros for every head (not `nan`).\n5. Concatenate heads in order to `(B, T_q, D)` and multiply by $W_o$.\n\n## Output\nFloat array `(B, T_q, D)`. No Python loops over batch, heads or positions.","starter":"import numpy as np\n\ndef gqa(Xq, Xkv, Wq, Wk, Wv, Wo, n_heads, n_kv_heads, kv_mask=None):\n    \"\"\"Return (B, Tq, D) grouped-query cross-attention output.\"\"\"\n    raise NotImplementedError\n","hints":["Project once, then reshape to heads: `(B, T, H, d_h)` transposed to `(B, H, T, d_h)` for queries, and `(B, H_kv, T_k, d_h)` for keys and values.","`np.repeat(K, H // H_kv, axis=1)` duplicates each KV head for its group of consecutive query heads (repeat, not tile: head order must be `g0, g0, g1, g1, ...`). From there it is ordinary batched attention.","Mask with `np.where(kv_mask[:, None, None, :], S, -inf)`. Before exponentiating, replace a non-finite row max by 0, and divide only where the row sum is positive so all-padding samples give zeros."],"sol":"import numpy as np\n\ndef gqa(Xq, Xkv, Wq, Wk, Wv, Wo, n_heads, n_kv_heads, kv_mask=None):\n    Xq, Xkv = np.asarray(Xq, dtype=float), np.asarray(Xkv, dtype=float)\n    B, Tq, D = Xq.shape\n    Tk = Xkv.shape[1]\n    H, G = n_heads, n_kv_heads\n    dh = D // H\n    Q = (Xq @ Wq).reshape(B, Tq, H, dh).transpose(0, 2, 1, 3)       # (B, H, Tq, dh)\n    K = (Xkv @ Wk).reshape(B, Tk, G, dh).transpose(0, 2, 1, 3)      # (B, G, Tk, dh)\n    V = (Xkv @ Wv).reshape(B, Tk, G, dh).transpose(0, 2, 1, 3)\n    K, V = np.repeat(K, H // G, axis=1), np.repeat(V, H // G, axis=1)   # head h -> kv head h // (H/G)\n    S = Q @ K.transpose(0, 1, 3, 2) / np.sqrt(dh)                     # (B, H, Tq, Tk)\n    if kv_mask is not None:\n        S = np.where(np.asarray(kv_mask)[:, None, None, :], S, -np.inf)\n    m = S.max(axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n    m = np.where(np.isfinite(m), m, 0.0)                             # all-padding rows\n    w = np.exp(S - m)\n    tot = w.sum(axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n    A = np.divide(w, tot, out=np.zeros_like(w), where=tot > 0)\n    O = (A @ V).transpose(0, 2, 1, 3).reshape(B, Tq, D)\n    return O @ Wo\n","ex_md":"## Why share keys and values\nAt decode time each new token must read the cached $K$ and $V$ of every previous token for every layer: $2 \\cdot L \\cdot T \\cdot H_{kv} d_h$ numbers. Memory bandwidth, not FLOPs, limits generation speed, so cutting $H_{kv}$ from 32 to 8 (Llama-2 70B) cuts the cache and the bytes read per token by 4x, with little quality loss. Queries are not cached, so keeping many query heads is cheap.\n\n## The head mapping\nConsecutive query heads share a KV head: with $H = 4$, $H_{kv} = 2$ the mapping is $0, 0, 1, 1$. `np.repeat` produces exactly that; `np.tile` would give $0, 1, 0, 1$ and silently pair the wrong heads. Production kernels avoid materialising the repeated tensor by reshaping queries to `(B, H_kv, H/H_kv, T, d_h)` instead.\n\n## Cross-attention and padding\nIn an encoder-decoder model the keys come from the encoder, so the mask is over **key** positions: padded source tokens must receive zero weight. A sample whose source is entirely padding (test 6) has nothing to attend to; returning zeros keeps `nan` from spreading through the residual stream.\n\n## Complexity\n$O(B H T_q T_k d_h)$ for the scores, the same as MHA; the saving is in the KV projections and cache, $H_{kv}/H$ of MHA's.\n\n## Interview follow-ups\n- How large is the KV cache of a 32-layer model with $H_{kv} = 8$, $d_h = 128$, a 32k context and fp16 values?\n- How would you convert a pretrained MHA checkpoint to GQA? (Mean-pool the K/V projection heads within each group, then fine-tune briefly.)","nex":2,"shown":[{"in":"array([[[1., 0.]]])\narray([[[1., 0.],\n        [0., 1.]]])\narray([[1., 0.],\n       [0., 1.]])\narray([[1., 0.],\n       [0., 1.]])\narray([[1., 0.],\n       [0., 1.]])\narray([[1., 0.],\n       [0., 1.]])\n1\n1","out":"array([[[0.66976155, 0.33023845]]])"},{"in":"array([[[1., 0.]]])\narray([[[1., 0.],\n        [0., 1.]]])\narray([[1., 0.],\n       [0., 1.]])\narray([[1.],\n       [0.]])\narray([[1.],\n       [0.]])\narray([[1., 0.],\n       [0., 1.]])\n2\n1\narray([[ True, False]])","out":"array([[[1., 1.]]])"}],"lessons":[{"href":"../ai-engineering-course/index.html#l05-02","t":"Multi-head attention","c":"AI Engineering"},{"href":"../inference-eng-course/index.html#l02-02","t":"Q, K, V & Causal Attention During Inference","c":"Inference Engineering"}],"related":["scaled-dot-product-attention-2","scaled-dot-product-attention","transformer-decoder-block"],"ntests":7,"tj":"[{\"a\": [{\"__nd__\": [[[1.0, 0.0]]], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, {\"__nd__\": [[[1.0, 0.0], [0.0, 1.0]]], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, {\"__nd__\": [[1.0, 0.0], [0.0, 1.0]], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, {\"__nd__\": [[1.0, 0.0], [0.0, 1.0]], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, {\"__nd__\": [[1.0, 0.0], [0.0, 1.0]], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, {\"__nd__\": [[1.0, 0.0], [0.0, 1.0]], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, 1, 1], \"e\": {\"__nd__\": [[[0.6697615493266569, 0.3302384506733431]]], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}}, {\"a\": [{\"__nd__\": [[[1.0, 0.0]]], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, {\"__nd__\": [[[1.0, 0.0], [0.0, 1.0]]], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, {\"__nd__\": [[1.0, 0.0], [0.0, 1.0]], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, {\"__nd__\": [[1.0], [0.0]], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, {\"__nd__\": [[1.0], [0.0]], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, {\"__nd__\": [[1.0, 0.0], [0.0, 1.0]], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}, 2, 1, {\"__nd__\": [[true, false]], \"dtype\": \"bool\"}], \"e\": {\"__nd__\": [[[1.0, 1.0]]], \"dtype\": \"float64\"}}, {\"a\": [{\"__nd__\": [[[-0.5119170007913422, -0.2739055692120024, 1.0750795529288018, 0.2979912406907926, 0.940662391915013, 0.3367676040403031, 0.5160863051316008, 0.11782752299215087], [0.5782355250445999, -0.8888127218457137, 1.0718376222496213, -1.1509674335283009, 0.15784276167685402, 0.015058731834308633, -0.6005366502354714, 0.34355858974614983], [-2.11071255121692, -0.9745260103945844, -0.10107949300979144, 0.7529999543568262, 0.927167330828724, -0.7339012426885787, -0.7767984992635784, -0.07100697522900477]], [[1.063565651995963, 0.8099123818647492, 0.3899573531095736, 0.6013687987430288, -0.4741300664246664, -1.9246753609727876, -0.1749057385228368, -0.5637760489963879], [-1.7366825994918076, -2.390859283799335, -0.2886985736621897, 0.6899596336875087, -0.5032220992412659, 0.4638343754930397, -1.8180108621569426, -0.7247939287582369], [1.5512279749334559, -0.24251595642883803, -0.3146905244638868, 0.21926397301194483, 0.584787378771336, -0.8177253308346331, 0.12064847709137766,